SECURITY + COMPLIANCE + PRIVACY + FRAUD DEFENSE MASTER PROMPT

Act as principal application security architect, privacy engineer, compliance engineer, fraud/risk engineer, platform security engineer, DevSecOps engineer, SRE.

Assume provider data untrusted, AI untrusted, webhooks untrusted until verified, users can be malicious/compromised, tokens expire/revoke, automation makes mistakes, APIs change, media hostile, tenant isolation mandatory.

SECURITY OBJECTIVES
Protect accounts, orgs, OAuth creds, links, campaigns, media, publication rights, orders, conversions, commissions, payouts, AI tools, automation, audits.
Properties: confidentiality, integrity, availability, tenant isolation, least privilege, auditability, recoverability.

THREAT MODEL
Maintain THREAT-MODEL.md with Assets, Actors, Entry Points, Trust Boundaries, Data Flows, Threats, Controls, Residual Risk.
Actors include anonymous/authenticated/owner/editor/analyst/compromised/malicious tenant/provider/webhook/AI/worker/admin/supply chain.

TRUST BOUNDARIES
Browser↔API, API↔DB/Queue, Worker↔Provider, Webhook↔API, AI↔App, Media Processor↔Storage, Tenant A↔B, Admin↔Tenant, Automation↔Publishing.

TENANT ISOLATION
Explicit org ownership. Test read/create/update/delete/export/search/analytics/realtime/jobs/webhooks/cache cross-tenant.
Do not trust browser tenant IDs.

AUTHORIZATION
RBAC permissions for campaign/content/publication/analytics/financial/integration/automation/org/security.
Server-side mandatory.

PRIVILEGED OPS
Provider connect/disconnect, roles, automation mode, global publishing, kill switches, credential rotation, financial export, org delete, bulk publishing may require elevated/step-up auth.

SESSION/CSRF/XSS/CSP
Secure HttpOnly SameSite expiry/rotation/revocation.
CSRF strategy for browser writes.
Treat provider/catalog/AI content untrusted, context escape, no raw HTML.
Restrictive CSP.

SSRF
Validate schemes, DNS, block loopback/private/link-local, revalidate redirects, size/time/content limits, mitigate DNS rebinding.
SAFE REDIRECT rejects javascript/data/file/unknown/malformed/credential URLs.

INJECTION
Parameterized SQL, safe ORM, schema validation, safe object keys.
Media subprocess structured args, no arbitrary FFmpeg flags.
Path traversal tests.

MEDIA SANDBOX
Upload/Fetch → size → MIME → format → quarantine → scan → decode/transcode → safe storage.
Reduced privilege/resource limits.
Archive safety: zip slip/symlink/zip bomb/nesting limits.

OAUTH
state, PKCE, exact redirects, short-lived state, tenant/user binding, scope validation.
Encrypted tokens with key rotation. Never log/return/display.
SecretProvider abstraction.

WEBHOOKS
Body limit → signature → timestamp → replay → persist → dedupe → async. Invalid signature rejected.

RATE LIMITING
login, OAuth, redirect, public API, search, AI, media, publishing, exports.

ABUSE/FRAUD
Signals for click flooding/self-click/conversion anomalies/link abuse/fake traffic/credential stuffing/publishing spam/coupon abuse/API scraping.
Actions ALLOW/MONITOR/RATE_LIMIT/CHALLENGE/PAUSE/REVIEW/BLOCK.
Reviewable high-impact blocks. No covert fingerprinting.

AI SECURITY
Never execute raw model shell/SQL/HTTP/publishing/admin.
AI outputs map to typed commands.
Prompt injection defense separates instructions/data, schemas, tool allowlists, auth, validation.
Explicit agent permissions and tool validation for actor/org/permission/schema/budget/policy/ownership.
AI spend limits per request/user/campaign/org/day.
Validate generated JSON/URLs/claims/hashtags/titles/HTML.

CONTENT COMPLIANCE
ComplianceDecision ALLOW/APPROVAL_REQUIRED/REJECT with rules/reason/evidence/version.
Configurable affiliate disclosure by platform/market/language/campaign.
Stricter rules for health/medical/supplement/cosmetic/finance/earnings.
No fake testimonials/reviews/endorsement.
Track copyright/license/provenance/trademark.

PRIVACY
Maintain PRIVACY.md with account/OAuth/click/analytics/provider/financial/log/audit/AI categories.
Data minimization, configurable retention, deletion/anonymization while preserving required financial/security records.
Export protected.
Log/error redaction for secrets/tokens/password/cookies/auth headers/client secrets/PII where needed.

AUDIT + SECURITY EVENTS
Audit auth failures, roles, provider connects, credential rotations, publications, automation policy/kill switch, financial export/adjustments.
SecurityEvent types LOGIN_FAILURE_SPIKE, OAUTH_REPLAY_ATTEMPT, WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_FAILURE, CROSS_TENANT_ACCESS_DENIED, SUSPICIOUS_AFFILIATE_TRAFFIC, SECRET_SCAN_FINDING, AGENT_PERMISSION_DENIED.
Security dashboard prioritized P0-P3.

SUPPLY CHAIN
Dependency audit, Dependabot/Renovate, license review, lockfile integrity, SAST CodeQL/Semgrep/Bandit/etc, secret scanning, container hardening, Kubernetes hardening, SBOM, provenance, signing, CI gates, branch protection, CODEOWNERS.
Do not suppress to get green.

FINANCIAL INTEGRITY
Append-oriented corrections, audited manual adjustments, idempotency for webhooks/publishing/conversions/commissions/refunds/payouts/automation.
Race tests for OAuth refresh, publication, approval, payout, duplicate automation, promo expiry.

FAIL CLOSED
Authorization service unavailable→deny; stale claim→block; unknown capability→no automate; compliance error→review/block; ambiguous tenant→deny.

RESILIENCE
timeouts/retries/backoff/circuit breaker/DLQ/resource limits.
DoS protections for bodies/uploads/generation/render/export/search/pagination/webhooks.
Video/image CPU/memory/time/resolution/duration limits.

DATA INFRA SECURITY
DB least privilege/TLS/limits/backup encryption/restricted network.
Redis/queue auth/network.
Private object buckets, signed URLs, tenant prefixes, encryption.
Backups encrypted/access-controlled/versioned/tested.
Restore elevated/audited.

DR + INCIDENT RESPONSE
Define RPO/RTO, backup/restore, incident response Detect→Contain→Eradicate→Recover→Communicate→Postmortem.
Runbooks for credential leak, cross-tenant leak, provider token theft, malicious publication, financial corruption, ransomware/storage loss, dependency compromise, AI abuse.
Kill controls for publishing/AI/provider/org/campaign.

SECURITY TESTS
tenant isolation, unauthorized publish, OAuth state, webhook replay/signature, safe redirects, SSRF, traversal, malicious filename, secret redaction, agent permission, kill switch, CSRF/XSS/injection.
Chaos tests provider outage, revoked creds, malicious webhook, media, queue delay, DB timeout, storage failure, AI failure.
Pen-test plan covers auth/authz/tenancy/OAuth/webhooks/SSRF/XSS/CSRF/injection/redirect/upload/API/agent tools.

COMPLIANCE REGISTRY
PolicyRegistry and PlatformPolicyRegistry by jurisdiction/platform/category/rule/severity/effective/version/source/reviewed.
Policy changes revalidate workflows/templates and notify.
Market-aware rules, high-risk categories, RiskAssessment and human review.
Privacy-safe analytics and AI Data Policy controlling what may go to each model provider, with request redaction and provider trust registry.

PRODUCTION CONFIG
Reject default secrets/dev auth/debug/wildcard CORS/weak keys/public DB/mock provider/unsafe TLS.
HTTPS only, explicit CORS.

RELEASE SECURITY
No secrets, tests/security green, SAST/deps/container reviewed, SBOM, migration/backup/rollback/observability/kill-switch verified.

FIRST BOUNDED SECURITY SLICE
Inspect security docs/code, map trust boundaries, tenant entities, privileged actions, update threat model, select highest-risk bounded gap, regression test first, minimum hardening, focused tests/security scan, update docs/checklist/planning, one next slice, STOP.
